				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1589,
				8
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Normalize IPC handler exports to Fn convention\n\nRename the three Cocoon IPC handler entry points from descriptive names (CocoonExtensionHostMessage, CocoonNotify, CocoonRequest) to the uniform `Fn` ident, and add the matching `as` aliases in the mod.rs re-exports so downstream callers are unaffected.\n\nAdd four new ExtensionHost IPC handlers also exporting as `Fn`:\n\n- **DebugServiceClose:** Emits `sky://exthost/debug-close` via Tauri's Emitter trait so Sky can react to debug-session teardown.\n- **DebugServiceReload:** Emits `SkyEvent::ExtHostDebugReload` as a typed event, giving Wind a signal to purge caches before Cocoon restarts.\n- **StarterCreate:** Returns a stub extension-host ID (`\"1\"`) to satisfy VS Code's extensionHostStarter:createExtensionHost protocol.\n- **StarterStart:** Returns the real Cocoon PID (via GetCocoonPid) or Mountain's own PID as fallback, enabling external debuggers to attach to the correct Node.js process.\n\nAll handler modules now follow a single convention: each file exposes `pub async fn Fn(...)` and is aliased at the mod.rs boundary. This eliminates naming guesswork when adding new IPC routes and keeps the interface consistent across all WindServiceHandlers.",
			"SHA": "67e95cb626157a0f6e1a5b4f9d23dc35bebbf124"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T10:30:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1585,
				4
			],
			"Message": "perf(Mountain): Cache getInstalled extension responses per type filter\n\nBuilding the serialized ILocalExtension[] array on every `extensions:getInstalled` IPC call re-serialized ~1.8 MB of extension metadata, visible as a multi-hundred-millisecond stall in the UI on startup. Add a `OnceLock`-backed static cache keyed by the three TypeFilter variants (None, System, User). The first call per type populates the cache; subsequent calls return the cached `Value` clone in <1 ms. Empty responses are not cached so a first-call timeout does not permanently poison the slot.\n\nAlso fix two reliability concerns in the same area:\n- **FileCloneNative:** Create the target parent directory via `tokio::fs::create_dir_all` before `fs::copy`. VS Code's local-history feature creates per-file history directories that may not exist yet, producing an OS-level ENOENT on clone.\n- **CocoonManagement IO forwarders:** Switch from `tokio::spawn` to `tauri::async_runtime::spawn` so the forwarder tasks live on Tauri's runtime handle and continue to be polled while the spawning async task is waiting elsewhere. Restructure the read loops from `while let Ok(Some(…))` to an explicit `loop` + `match` that handles EOF and read errors instead of silently dropping the pipe. Log a warning when a pipe handle is `None` (indicating `Stdio::piped()` was not configured), aiding debug of silent IO loss.\n\n**tauri.conf.json:** Add `Proto/Vine.proto` to the resource bundle so the .proto file is available at runtime from `Contents/Resources/` alongside the other bundled assets.",
			"SHA": "a83e88eefa539b9b5bc7582822125fb8f7114d58"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T08:38:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1585,
				9
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Clean up dead vars and normalize scan paths lexically\n\nReplace the filesystem-backed `Canonicalize` closure in ScanPathConfigure\nwith `Normalize`, which resolves `..` segments lexically for non-existent\npaths - keeping extension scan-path log output clean regardless of path\nviability - while still calling `std::fs::canonicalize` for existing paths\nto resolve symlinks.\n\nDrop the stale `HandleSlot` accumulator in OutputChannelCoalesce (it was\nset but never meaningfully used after the previous refactor) and the\nunused `std::path::PathBuf` import in TryShipped.\n\nAdd stub IPC handlers for `browserView:*` (updateKeybindings, updateTheme,\nupdateConfiguration, openDevTools, closeDevTools -> Null;\ngetBrowserViews -> []), which Wind sends for Electron BrowserView\nmanagement but are no-ops under Tauri's single-webview architecture.\nRoute `extensionHostStarter:waitForExit` to a new async handler that\nresolves immediately with a stub exit-info so callers don't hang.\n\nFormatting-only: line-break Cocoon environment allow list one-per-entry,\ncollapse LocalhostUrl accessors, reflow WebviewWindowBuilder chain.",
			"SHA": "167dfea1480a374254428bcbbafa11c6113041c5"
		}
	],
